==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Twinstars, type Φ''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Divine Twinstars Φ''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Twinstars are not the best generalists due to their health, but let them loose on any [[:Category:XP Guerrilla Stages|XP Stage]] and they will demolish everything. Just make sure to keep them well protected with your meatshields or they will most likely get knocked back before attacking. They are generally not great at quickly killing units that have a wide range or many knockbacks, but, thanks to their Multi-Hit ability, they are one of the best units for peon control and are also able to keep Dark pushers at bay by knocking them back every time a foe comes charging.

In stages like [[Gestalt, Decay]], they are one of the best units to use as they can juggle enemies, stalling their approach via brute force. They have better range than many small units and are more cost-efficient, so it depends on the stage. Twinstars work very well in [[Into the Future]] and [[Cats of the Cosmos]] too, although the lack of abilities to counter [[:Category:Starred Alien Enemies|Starred Aliens]] specifically prevents them from being universally good in the latter.

Unfortunately, despite having higher range than rushers like Awakened Bahamut, they lack a high damage per hit even with [[Massive Damage|Massive Damage]] and usually miss multiple attacks sequentially due to their Multi-Hit ability. This often means even against their targeted traits, they can struggle and sometimes perform no better than generalists.

==='''True Form'''===
Divine Twinstars Φ gain slightly higher damage, higher movement speed, reduced recharge time, and immunity to Weaken. This makes them much more useful in their own niche, doing better than what they're already good at, but doesn't necessarily improve the most. Nevertheless, they still can be used as powerful specialists, having the range to back it up.

==='''Talents'''===
Basic stat boosts, as with most stat-based units, are helpful, but only after a significant investment with [[Catseye]]s if you really lack better specialists. Twinstars can perform well, but are more of a mediocre unit and the NP could be spent elsewhere.

'''[[Immune to Curse|Curse Immunity]]''' does not serve them well, as there are much better ways to deal with their targeted traits, even if curse sources are factored in. Furthermore, most curse-inflicting enemies deal extreme damage and have massive health, which are the very things they cannot handle. '''[[Slow|Slow]]''', while consistent with their multi-hits, is also unnecessary, as superior options exist in their targeted traits, and being a unit that specializes dealing damage, it's better to kill them outright, leaving the crowd control for others. '''[[Special Abilities#Resist|Resist Wave]]''' is just straight-up useless for fragile units like them.

==='''Ultra Talents'''===
Divine Twinstars Φ' Ultra Talents vary heavily in usefulness.

Your main priority should always be the '''[[Savage Blow|Savage Blow]]''' ability, increasing their DPS by a whopping 1.6x up to ~60,000 even without Attack Buff Talents. At such a fast attack rate, this makes them even more proficient at juggling and killing Dark enemies, while gearing them up to be an extremely powerful ranged rusher against many of the tanky frontline Alien pushers like [[General GreGory]] and [[Star Peng]]. The attack boost, if it activates, effectively lets them deal their full attack cycle's damage of 215,040 in a single hit.

Their other two Ultra Talents, on the other hand, are borderline unnecessary. '''[[Immune to Slow]]''' is niche at best, and hardly sees any applicability against enemies that won't already juggle them to death. You don't want Divine Twinstars Φ getting hit to begin with, and this Talent hardly does anything to help with their survivability even in the case that they do get inflicted with status effects. It can aid them against [[Le'Grim]], or [[Crustaceous Scissorex]], but that's as far as it goes.

'''Cost Down''' is a simple quality-of-life improvement that decreases their cost by a measly ~19.2%. As an Ultra Talent, it is exorbitantly expensive in terms of NP and seeks to resolve an issue they don't have. It is nonetheless a genuine improvement to the unit, so this Talent should be your second priority if you have the excess funds.

Overall, Twinstars see a moderate improvement to their overall performance, but still suffers in terms of survivability. Their niche is also questionable by the stage of the game you unlock these Ultra Talents in, so invest at your own discretion.

